des at start, quit, SIGTERM and with the flag off; wheel and click screens; clicks on the approval buttons send nothing). Limitations: no suspend handling exists (Ctrl+Z is a plain key with the terminal in raw mode; an external SIGTSTP leaves the modes on while stopped, as it does raw mode and the alternate screen); the panic path is code-level only (not exercised in the pty); a terminal that ignores 1000/1006 gets no mouse and keeps its native wheel behaviour; tmux needs `set -g mouse on` to pass events through and was not run; the card highlight is a colour, covered by the unit tests, not by the text dumps. |
