k installed after ratatui's (so before the message prints) and by the stop watchdog before it force-exits; around the sidecar shutdown, input in flight is drained before and after it and the tty input queue is flushed (`tcflush`) before cooked mode returns, so reports do not reach the shell. A split report on a high-latency link can still leave `Esc` plus stray characters (documented; `NEXUS_TUI_MOUSE=off` is the remedy); wheel notches queued together scroll once per redraw. Text selection: hold Shift (Option in iTerm2 and macOS Terminal) while dragging; the app does no selection of its own. Captures: `docs/evidence/v1.1.4/tui/D-10/` (modes at start, quit, SIGTERM and with the flag off; wheel and click screens; clicks on the approval buttons send nothing). Limitations: no suspend handling exists (Ctrl+Z is a plain key with the terminal in raw mode; an external SIGTSTP leaves the modes on while stopped, as it does raw mode and the alternate screen); the panic path is code-level only (not exercised in the pty); a terminal that ignores 1000/1006 gets no mouse and keeps its native wheel behaviour; tmux needs `set -g mouse on` to pass events through and was not run; the card highlight is a colour, covered by the unit tests, not by the text dumps. |
